    <div class="row">
      
      <div class="col-md-12">
     
        <p class="mb-0">E-Date has received information that the members of public have been receiving spurious calls, instant messages and phishing emails from un-identified persons/ entities such as hrE-Date.com, posing to be our employee or authorised agents. The imposters are using highly deceptive email ID and website domains, and even our branding and logos, to falsify their identity and impersonate us. The imposters are offering lucrative jobs and discounted services, and are luring the users and public into providing sensitive data such as personally identifiable information, banking and credit card details, and passwords.
</p>
          <p>E-Date  cautions its users and public at large against such unsolicited calls, instant messages and emails and requests:</p>
          <ol>
              <li>To check, verify and confirm the genuineness of the message/ communication received from any source, making any such offer on behalf of E-Date;</li>
              <li>Not to share any personal or sensitive information, with any unidentified or unverified person, to avoid risk of being scammed;</li>
              <li>Not to respond to any unsolicited call or message or click on any unverified link or attachment;</li>
          </ol>
        
          <p>
         We provide correct and proper information of our products, services and jobs on our website www.edateworld.com or our official social media handles as mentioned on the website. If you have any doubts about a request or communication, contact us directly at <a href="#">contact@www.edateworld.com</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
